From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Keep the screen sharing permission for the login session inside Flatpak

Patch 0006 stores the portal's restore token in the runtime directory, so a
cast is not asked which screen to share again during the same login session.
Inside a Flatpak sandbox the runtime directory is created anew every time the
application starts, so the token was lost when the application closed and the
portal asked again on the next start.

Flatpak keeps $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/app/$FLATPAK_ID for the whole login session and
shares it between starts of the application. Inside a sandbox the token is now
stored there, so it lasts exactly as long as it does outside one. Outside a
sandbox nothing changes.

diff -ruN a/src/stream/nd-stream.c b/src/stream/nd-stream.c
--- a/src/stream/nd-stream.c
+++ b/src/stream/nd-stream.c
@@ -276,10 +276,25 @@
  * the chooser of the attempt before it, which the user sees as "Screencast
  * canceled" and as being asked the same question over and over. The token is
  * kept in the runtime directory, so it lasts for the login session and no
- * longer. */
+ * longer.
+ *
+ * Inside a Flatpak sandbox the runtime directory is created anew for every
+ * start of the application, which would forget the token each time. Flatpak
+ * keeps $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/app/$FLATPAK_ID for the whole login session instead,
+ * so the token goes there and lasts exactly as long as it does outside. */
 static gchar *
 nd_stream_restore_token_path (void)
 {
+  const gchar *flatpak_id = g_getenv ("FLATPAK_ID");
+
+  if (flatpak_id && flatpak_id[0] != '\0' &&
+      g_file_test ("/.flatpak-info", G_FILE_TEST_EXISTS))
+    return g_build_filename (g_get_user_runtime_dir (),
+                             "app",
+                             flatpak_id,
+                             "screencast-restore-token",
+                             NULL);
+
   return g_build_filename (g_get_user_runtime_dir (),
                            "mirdispo",
                            "screencast-restore-token",
